meta {
  name: List volunteers dropdown
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/lookup/volunteers
  body: none
  auth: none
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # List Volunteers Dropdown

  Returns a lightweight list of accepted volunteer registrations for use in mentorship assignment dropdown/select components. Each entry contains only the volunteer `id`, `name` (first name + surname) and `status`.

  ## Authorization
  No authentication required. This is a public lookup endpoint.

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`** — Returns an array of `{ id, name, status }` objects for accepted volunteers. name is a concatenation of firstName and surname from the queried database table. 

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "students found successfully",
    "data": [
      { "id": "uuid", "name": "Bob Zayne", "status": "accepted" }
    ],
    "meta": {
      "correlationId": "uuid-v4-string"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Caching
  Response is cached under `cedarrise:lookup:volunteers` with `LISTS` TTL (10 mins).

  ## Errors

  | Status                      | Description              |
  |-----------------------------|--------------------------|
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error. |
}
